A||N||3||FieroHarry||Deck lid power supply ?||||9||
Z||000000||FieroHarry||04-22-2001||03:25 PM||||Hey gang,<BR>Silly question time.<BR>At one time some idiot disconnected the power lead for the trunk release sol. on my 85GT. The wire is hangin out the forward edge of the deck lid but cant seem to find what it was connected to before.<BR>Some other 87 and 88's ive looked at have the power lead run on the passenger side where mine is on the drivers side.<BR>DOes anybody know whether mine is run wrong and what color lead am I looking for?<P>I help in this would really be appreciated.<BR><P>------------------<BR>Harry<BR>FOCOSEVA<BR>1985 GT 258K+ "TEMPTATION"||||reg||9
Z||000001||theogre||04-22-2001||03:27 PM||||I'm not sure on 85 which side it's on. sounds like someone may have swapped the lid on you. (The 4 terminal weatherpack connector on the 86+ is hard to miss.) ||||reg||1
Z||000002||FieroHarry||04-22-2001||03:30 PM||||I chased the VIN before and its a fully loaded factory gt with all the bells and whistles. I dont see any 4 prong connector anywhere back there<P>------------------<BR>Harry<BR>FOCOSEVA<BR>1985 GT 258K+ "TEMPTATION"||||reg||1
Z||000003||FieroJoe||04-22-2001||10:07 PM||||If it is in fact supposed to be on the left side of the trunk lid, and nothing was swapped, there should be another wire just hanging down by the hinge that it was originally attached to.<P>There probably was a connector too, look for the other end of a plastic connector.  I assume this wire would also probably be in some sort of loom or corrugated tubing to protect it from exhaust heat.<P>You might have to go diggin, but I bet there's something down there!<P>------------------<BR>AIM: Fiero87311<BR>87 Coupe 5sp. - big resto near completion!<BR>     <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/profile_1.JPG">  <p>[This message has been edited by FieroJoe (edited 04-22-2001).]||||reg||1
